<title>USA: TB Wood's Q3 net rises, shr falls.</title>
<headline>TB Wood's Q3 net rises, shr falls.</headline>
<dateline>CHAMBERSBURG, Pa. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>TB WOOD'S CORPORATION</p>
<p>						 Quarter Ended</p>
<p>					 9/27/96    9/29/95(A)</p>
<p> Net Sales		     $25,849,000   $25,263,000</p>
<p> Net Income			1,684,000     1,196,000</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share		   0.29	    0.31</p>
<p> AVG Shares Outstanding	5,851,000     3,832,000</p>
<p>					   Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>					 9/27/96    9/29/95(A)</p>
<p> Net Sales			74,769,000    77,792,000</p>
<p>Net Income before</p>
<p>Non-recurring Charge and</p>
<p>    Extraordinary Item	 4,481,000     3,404,000</p>
<p> Non-recurring Charge	 349,000(B)		--</p>
<p>Net Income before</p>
<p>    Extraordinary Item	 4,132,000     3,404,000</p>
<p> Extraordinary Item	 1,305,000(C)		--</p>
<p> Net Income			2,827,000     3,404,000</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share Before</p>
<p>Non-recurring Charge</p>
<p>    &amp; Extraordinary Item	    0.81	    0.88</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share before  Extraordinary Item		   0.75	    0.88</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share after</p>
<p>Non-recurring Charge</p>
<p>    &amp; Extraordinary Item	    0.51	    0.88</p>
<p> AVG Shares Outstanding	5,501,000     3,868,000</p>
<p>(A) Earnings per share information is based on pre-IPO shares outstanding and is not comparable to current year results</p>
<p>(B) Non-recurring charge of $349,000 net of taxes related to the write-off of a non-compete agreement in February 1996.</p>
<p>(C) Early extinguishment of debt related to initial public offering of $1,305,000 (net of taxes) in February 1996.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
